## Summary

Delivered a native **SwiftUI / Apple-HIG `MQTTInspectorPage`** at full parity with the web source (`web/src/features/telemetry/pages/MQTTInspectorPage.tsx`), adaptive across macOS + iOS, with **`PARITY_COVERED=41/41`**.

**New surface** (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Telemetry/`, 8 files):
- `MQTTInspectorPage.swift` — adaptive page scaffold (ScrollView, nav title, onAppear/Disappear lifecycle)
- `.Projection.swift` — pure Foundation core: DTOs, totals reduces, stale rule (120s), the throughput `useEffect` port, `formatUptime`/`formatRelative`/`fmtInt`, i18n facade, a11y summary
- `.Model.swift` — `@Observable MQTTInspectorPageModel` over a pure-Swift `/telemetry` seam (no `import Shared`); loading/empty/error/content phases + live freshness
- `.Views.swift` / `.Table.swift` — all **8 panels** (error banner, 4 StatCards, connection-info, **Swift Charts `TSAreaChart`** throughput, adaptive vehicle table)
- `.Registration.swift`, `.Previews.swift` (5 states), `.Tests.swift` (19 tests)

**Wiring** (navigation registration + catalog): registered `.telemetry` route, added `/mqtt-inspector` deep-link alias, registered `TeslaSync/Features` in both app targets, and added **35 `mqtt.*` keys** (29 parity + 6 native, verbatim web values) to `Localizable.xcstrings`.

**Verification — all in-scope gates green:**
| Gate | Result |
|---|---|
| swiftc -typecheck **macOS 15** (Swift 6, strict concurrency) | 0 errors |
| swiftc -typecheck **iOS 18 sim** | 0 errors |
